Here's our payment provider webhook handler. Anything wrong with the signature verification or replay handling?

```js
app.use(express.json());

app.post('/webhooks/payments', async (req, res) => {
  const sig = req.get('X-Signature');
  if (sig) {
    const expected = crypto
      .createHmac('sha256', process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET)
      .update(JSON.stringify(req.body))
      .digest('hex');
    if (sig !== expected) return res.sendStatus(401);
  }
  if (req.body.type === 'payment.succeeded') {
    await Order.update({ status: 'paid' }, { where: { id: req.body.data.orderId } });
  }
  res.sendStatus(200);
});
```

The provider also sends an X-Timestamp header and an event id in the body; we don't use either.

